  "starterCode": "# Interleaved RoPE + NoPE — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(x, positions, rotary_pairs):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Interleaved RoPE + NoPE** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, positions, rotary_pairs):\n    x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float); out=x.copy()\n    pairs=int(rotary_pairs)\n    if pairs<0 or 2*pairs>x.shape[-1]: raise ValueError(\"rotary_pairs out of range\")\n    if pairs:\n        dim=2*pairs; sub=x[...,:dim]; pos=np.asarray(positions,dtype=float)\n        inv=1/(10000.0**(np.arange(0,dim,2,dtype=float)/dim)); ang=pos[...,None]*inv\n        c,s=np.cos(ang),np.sin(ang)\n        out[...,:dim:2]=sub[...,0::2]*c-sub[...,1::2]*s\n        out[...,1:dim:2]=sub[...,0::2]*s+sub[...,1::2]*c\n    return out.tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
